          "id": "c75f94227c7962b78cbaa5ea188db3f101ed8bc5",
          "message": "{Tests} Remove fallback polling waits from offline scenarios (#1127)\n\n**Related command**\n<!-- If applicable, provide the related command, for example: az vm\ncreate, az login, or Az.Compute. -->\n\nDeployment and VM creation offline scenarios (CLI and PowerShell)\n\n**Description**\n<!-- Why this PR? What changed? What is the user or maintainer impact?\n-->\n\nOffline tests mock HTTP but still wait for the engine's hard-coded\n**15-second polling interval**.\n\nThis temporary workaround adds an environment variable\n`TEMP_AZCLIPS_PLAYBACK_TEST_POLLING_INTERVAL`. `ScenarioHost`\nautomatically sets it to `0` offline, clears it for live/record hosts\n(`useLiveAuth: true`), and restores the previous value afterward.\nTransparent to developers.\n\nRemove the fake VM backend's blanket `Retry-After: 1`, which otherwise\noverrides the zero fallback. The playback-neutralization test adds a\nnonzero header after recording, preserving coverage without\nrecording-time waits. Production headers and live polling are unchanged.\n\n**Observed impact:**\n\nFrom\n<img width=\"1088\" height=\"1796\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0e596065-846f-4e45-8b4e-80715438862a\"\n/>\n\nTo\n<img width=\"1084\" height=\"1789\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a492933-65f1-4d6b-a059-67cfa8f112fd\"\n/>\n\n\n- One deployment invocation: **~15 s → 146 ms CLI / 8 ms PowerShell**.\n- VM size test: **4 s → 3 ms**; accelerated-networking test: **12 s → 12\nms**.\n- Full run: **310.7 s → 51.26 s (~84% faster)**; **2,984 passed, 10\nskipped, 0 failed**.\n\nTimings compare development runs, not a controlled benchmark; test\ncounts differ.\n\n**Testing Guide**\n<!-- List validation commands or manual test steps. -->\n\n- `dotnet build azclips.slnx --no-restore --verbosity quiet` — passed\n(existing warnings).\n- `dotnet test tests/Scenario.Tests/Scenario.Tests.csproj --no-restore\n--filter 'FullyQualifiedName~VmCreateOrchestrationTests' --logger\n'console;verbosity=normal'` — all 73 passed, including\nplayback-neutralization and swapped-order coverage.\n- `dotnet test azclips.slnx --no-restore --verbosity minimal` — 2,984\npassed, 10 skipped, 0 failed; 51.26 s wall-clock time.\n\n\n\n**History Notes**\n<!--\nRelease notes are generated from PR metadata during stable release\npreparation.\n\nUse [Component Name] for customer-facing changes that should appear in\nrelease notes.\nUse {Component Name} for internal, test-only, docs-only, or\nrelease-process changes that should not appear in release notes.\n\nPR titles must not end with trailing punctuation or trailing spaces.\n\nIf one PR needs multiple release-note entries, or if the PR title is\nonly a summary, add notes below in this format:\n\n[Component Name] `az command`: Add customer-facing behavior\n[Component Name] BREAKING CHANGE: `az command`: Remove deprecated\nbehavior\n\nHistory note lines must not end with trailing punctuation or trailing\nspaces.\n\nCommon components: CLI, PowerShell, Agent, Auth, Packaging, DevOps,\nDocs.\nDelete this section only when no release note is needed.\n-->\n\n{Tests} Remove fallback polling waits from offline scenarios\n\n---\n\n- [x] The PR title starts with `[Component Name]` for customer-facing\nchanges or `{Component Name}` for non-customer-facing changes, and does\nnot end with trailing punctuation or spaces.\n- [ ] Customer-facing changes include a useful release note in the PR\ntitle or the **History Notes** section.\n- [x] I added or updated tests for behavior changes.\n- [x] I updated documentation when behavior, setup, support, or security\nguidance changed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>",
