          "id": "fdd25b797bbd628730aad4767fbb8df0cb12c229",
          "message": "[Auth] Add service principal client-secret authentication (#1210)\n\n**Related command**\n<!-- If applicable, provide the related command, for example: az vm\ncreate, az login, or Az.Compute. -->\n`az login`, `Connect-AzAccount`\n\n**Description**\n<!-- Why this PR? What changed? What is the user or maintainer impact?\n-->\nAdd service principal authentication with a client secret across CLI and\nPowerShell.\n\n- Support `az login --client-secret` and PowerShell `-ClientSecret\n<SecureString>`, including backward-compatible `-ServicePrincipal\n-Credential <PSCredential>` syntax.\n- Add the shared client-secret authenticator, secret persistence, and\nprofile re-authentication support.\n- Refactor authentication request construction and credential handling,\nwith subscription lookup and validation coverage.\n- Update login help, profile documentation, exported help fixtures, and\nthe PowerShell changelog.\n\nFor a complete list of tech debts / gaps pls refer to\nhttps://microsoft.sharepoint.com/:fl:/g/contentstorage/CSP_2e24e7fe-1ac4-440f-bfce-2f4be2ac6e50/IQAn91UVJvRvTKAxz-vcn6ssAQuuZOx3P1u6jjzVM_YyNks?e=42Zfg2&%3D%3D\n\n**Testing Guide**\n<!-- List validation commands or manual test steps. -->\nValidated with the pinned .NET SDK 10.0.402:\n\n```bash\ndotnet test tests/Cli.Tests/Cli.Tests.csproj --no-restore --filter 'FullyQualifiedName~ServicePrincipalSecret|FullyQualifiedName~SubscriptionServiceLookup|FullyQualifiedName~ManagedIdentityCredential|FullyQualifiedName~ManagedIdentityIdCodec|FullyQualifiedName~MsalClientOptions|FullyQualifiedName~FederatedTokenCache|FullyQualifiedName~ProfileCli|FullyQualifiedName~ManagedIdentityE2E' --verbosity quiet\n```\nPassed: 134 passed, 4 skipped, 0 failed. The first attempt encountered\nconcurrent-build file contention; the sequential retry passed. Build\nwarnings were emitted.\n\n```bash\ndotnet test tests/Cmdlets.Tests/Cmdlets.Tests.csproj --no-restore --filter 'FullyQualifiedName~ConnectAccountCmdletTests|FullyQualifiedName~LoginProcessor' --verbosity quiet\n```\nPassed: 182 passed, 0 skipped, 0 failed.\n\nThe full solution build, remaining test suites, and live Azure\nauthentication were not run.\n\n**History Notes**\n<!--\nRelease notes are generated from PR metadata during stable release\npreparation.\n\nUse [Component Name] for customer-facing changes that should appear in\nrelease notes.\nUse {Component Name} for internal, test-only, docs-only, or\nrelease-process changes that should not appear in release notes.\n\nPR titles must not end with trailing punctuation or trailing spaces.\n\nIf one PR needs multiple release-note entries, or if the PR title is\nonly a summary, add notes below in this format:\n\n[Component Name] `az command`: Add customer-facing behavior\n[Component Name] BREAKING CHANGE: `az command`: Remove deprecated\nbehavior\n\nHistory note lines must not end with trailing punctuation or trailing\nspaces.\n\nCommon components: CLI, PowerShell, Agent, Auth, Packaging, DevOps,\nDocs.\nDelete this section only when no release note is needed.\n-->\n[CLI] `az login`: Add service principal client-secret authentication and\nsaved-profile re-authentication\n[PowerShell] `Connect-AzAccount`: Add service principal client-secret\nauthentication with SecureString and PSCredential support\n\n---\n\n- [x] The PR title starts with `[Component Name]` for customer-facing\nchanges or `{Component Name}` for non-customer-facing changes, and does\nnot end with trailing punctuation or spaces.\n- [x] Customer-facing changes include a useful release note in the PR\ntitle or the **History Notes** section.\n- [x] I added or updated tests for behavior changes.\n- [x] I updated documentation when behavior, setup, support, or security\nguidance changed.",
