          "id": "55759dcc95e3db1b88e6bf6bb288084fabdec8ef",
          "message": "[Auth] Move profiles and authentication caches to ~/.azclips (#1238)\n\n**Related command**\n<!-- If applicable, provide the related command, for example: az vm\ncreate, az login, or Az.Compute. -->\nN/A\n\n**Description**\n<!-- Why this PR? What changed? What is the user or maintainer impact?\n-->\n\nThis PR adds a persistence layer, namely the `IPersistenceStore`\ninterface and the `FilePersistenceStore` implementation. As a service or\ncommand, you can get the injected `IPersistenceStore` instance and do\nthe following things:\n\n- Gets the root path for persistence (honors `HomePaths`, i.e.\n`~/.azclips` by default, can be overridden by env var)\n- Resolves a relative path\n- File/directory IO\n\nAn example is `ProfileService`, it declares the dependency to\n`IPersistenceStore` in the constructor, and use the file I/O API for\npersisting the profiles.\n\n\nhttps://github.com/Azure/azclips/blob/596465b5702696fb1bec417b6f53962d8939cccf/src/Core/Core.Runtime/ProfileService.cs#L14\n\n\nhttps://github.com/Azure/azclips/blob/596465b5702696fb1bec417b6f53962d8939cccf/src/Core/Core.Runtime/ProfileService.cs#L202\n\n## Remarks\n\n1. Note that the persistence layer is designed to be able to store any\ndata (not only text, hence the `ReadOnlyMemory<byte>` type, but to make\nlife easier two extension methods were added with string as\ninput/output, such as **ReadTextAsync** in the above example.\n2. Another reason for introducing this layer is for testability, i.e.\nmocking file IO when testing for better perf / isolation.\n\n---the following is generated by AI----\n\n- Move profiles, the active-profile pointer, and authentication cache\nfiles to `~/.azclips`, alongside config and extensions, while preserving\n`AZCLIPS_HOME`.\n- Add `IPersistenceStore` in Core.Abstractions and its filesystem\nimplementation in Core.Runtime. Provide byte-oriented async reads,\natomic writes, directory creation, and deletion with cancellation\nsupport and private Unix permissions.\n- Inject persistence into profiles, MSAL cache setup, service principal\nsecret storage, and the TUI prompt. Core.Authentication does not depend\non Core.Runtime; secret-store APIs expose neither storage nor logging\ndependencies.\n- Update CLI/PowerShell documentation, isolated test and benchmark\nwiring, and regression coverage.\n\nExisting files under `{LocalApplicationData}/.azclips` are **not\nautomatically migrated or read**. Users must sign in again or move their\nstate manually. MSAL Keychain/libsecret/DPAPI protection and\ncredential-store identifiers remain unchanged. Config, extensions,\ntelemetry, and Agent storage are otherwise unchanged.\n\n**Testing Guide**\n<!-- List validation commands or manual test steps. -->\nValidated on macOS using the SDK pinned in `global.json`\n(`$HOME/.dotnet/dotnet`):\n\n- Solution build: passed, 0 warnings and 0 errors\n- Focused CLI tests: 392 passed\n- Focused PowerShell tests: 106 passed\n- Focused Agent tests: 10 passed\n- `git diff --check`: passed\n\nExact validation commands:\n```bash\n$HOME/.dotnet/dotnet build azclips.slnx --no-restore --verbosity quiet\n$HOME/.dotnet/dotnet test tests/Cli.Tests/Cli.Tests.csproj --no-build --no-restore --filter 'FullyQualifiedName~PersistenceStoreTests|FullyQualifiedName~ProfileServiceTests|FullyQualifiedName~MsalClientOptionsTests|FullyQualifiedName~FederatedTokenCacheTests|FullyQualifiedName~ServicePrincipalSecretStoreTests|FullyQualifiedName~ServicePrincipalSecretTokenTests|FullyQualifiedName~ServicePrincipalSecretAuthenticatorTests|FullyQualifiedName~EncryptionFallbackWarningTests|FullyQualifiedName~MsalAuthTelemetryTests|FullyQualifiedName~ProfileCliTests|FullyQualifiedName~ManagedIdentityE2ETests|FullyQualifiedName~BenchmarkProfileStoreTests|FullyQualifiedName~GetAccessTokenCliBindingTests|FullyQualifiedName~GroupDeleteTests|FullyQualifiedName~GroupExistsTests|FullyQualifiedName~GroupUpdateTests|FullyQualifiedName~IdentityExtensionTests|FullyQualifiedName~ResourceGroupDeploymentCliTests|FullyQualifiedName~RoleAssignmentCliTests|FullyQualifiedName~RoleAssignmentCreateTests|FullyQualifiedName~RoleAssignmentDeleteTests|FullyQualifiedName~ConfigCliTests' --verbosity quiet\n$HOME/.dotnet/dotnet test tests/Cmdlets.Tests/Cmdlets.Tests.csproj --no-build --no-restore --filter 'FullyQualifiedName~LoginProcessorClientSecretTests|FullyQualifiedName~ConnectAccountCmdletTests|FullyQualifiedName~GetAccessTokenCmdletTests|FullyQualifiedName~ManagedServiceIdentityCmdletTests|FullyQualifiedName~ResourceGroupDeploymentCmdletTests' --verbosity quiet\n$HOME/.dotnet/dotnet test Agent/tests/Core.Agent.Tests/Core.Agent.Tests.csproj --no-build --no-restore --filter 'FullyQualifiedName~DirectReadEnvironmentTests|FullyQualifiedName~DirectReadCommandTests.EnvProcessorMatchesDirectProvider' --verbosity quiet\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nFull test suites and Windows/Linux validation were not run.\n\n**History Notes**\n<!--\nRelease notes are generated from PR metadata during stable release\npreparation.\n\nUse [Component Name] for customer-facing changes that should appear in\nrelease notes.\nUse {Component Name} for internal, test-only, docs-only, or\nrelease-process changes that should not appear in release notes.\n\nPR titles must not end with trailing punctuation or trailing spaces.\n\nIf one PR needs multiple release-note entries, or if the PR title is\nonly a summary, add notes below in this format:\n\n[Component Name] `az command`: Add customer-facing behavior\n[Component Name] BREAKING CHANGE: `az command`: Remove deprecated\nbehavior\n\nHistory note lines must not end with trailing punctuation or trailing\nspaces.\n\nCommon components: CLI, PowerShell, Agent, Auth, Packaging, DevOps,\nDocs.\nDelete this section only when no release note is needed.\n-->\n[Auth] BREAKING CHANGE: Move profile and authentication cache files to\n`~/.azclips`; files in the previous local application data directory are\nnot migrated automatically\n\n---\n\n- [x] The PR title starts with `[Component Name]` for customer-facing\nchanges or `{Component Name}` for non-customer-facing changes, and does\nnot end with trailing punctuation or spaces.\n- [x] Customer-facing changes include a useful release note in the PR\ntitle or the **History Notes** section.\n- [x] I added or updated tests for behavior changes.\n- [x] I updated documentation when behavior, setup, support, or security\nguidance changed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>",
